                {
                    "type": "heading",
                    "text": "Scale"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Most people can build a doghouse\nTraditionally people built their own homes\nPerhaps with help from experienced village people\nStill happens in many places in the world\nNobody just goes and builds a skyscraper\nDraw plans (incl. market) and organize it all\nMake sure construction is solid\nAbide by earthquake regulations ( כפוף לרגולציה)\nThis is a work for professionals"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "page_number": 20,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "heading",
                    "text": "What Engineers Can Do"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Predict system behavior\ne.g. conditions leading to stability or instability\nCalculate design tolerances\nIs manufacturing variation still OK?\nCalculate failure probability\nChances that change in conditions will be really bad"
                },
                {
                    "type": "heading",
                    "text": "Use all this to extend previous systems"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Skyscrapers, jumbo jets, and supercomputers represent accumulated knowledge over many years"
                },
                {
                    "type": "heading",
                    "text": "This is way beyond what any virtuoso ever did"
                }
            ]
